{{also|nudel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Attested since 16th century, further origin {{unk|de|title=unknown}}. Perhaps from a variant of {{m|de|Knödel}},<ref>{{R:de:EWbD|Nudel}}</ref> such as [[Silesian]] {{der|de|gmw-ecg|knudel}}. The unusual loss of ''k-'' is apparently attested in {{cog|vls|noedel|t=dumpling}}. If already {{der|de|dum|-}}, such a dialectal form might have been brought to eastern Germany by Flemish settlers. (Standard {{cog|nl|noedel}} stems from the German.)

An alternative theory derives it from {{bor|de|lld|menudli|t=small piece of dough found in soup}}, from {{der|de|la|minutulus}}, diminutive of {{m|la|minūtus|t=diminished, diminutive, lessened}}.

